T$-decomposition of a graph $G$ is a set of edge-disjoint copies of $T$ in $G$ that cover the edge set of $G$. Graham and Häggkvist (1989) conjectured that any $2\\ell$-regular graph $G$ admits a $T$-decomposition if $T$ is a tree with $\\ell$ edges. Kouider and Lonc (1999) conjectured that, in the special case where $T$ is the path with $\\ell$ edges, $G$ admits a $T$-decomposition $\\mathcal{D}$ where every vertex of $G$ is the end-vertex of exactly two paths of $\\mathcal{D}$, and proved that this statement holds when $G$ has girth at least $(\\ell+3)/2$. In this paper we verify Kouider and Lonc's Conjecture for paths of length $4$. △ Less\n\nSubmitted 5 July, 2016; originally announced July 2016.\n\nMSC Class: 05B40; 05C70; 05C51; 05C38\n\n  17. arXiv:1510.02526  [pdf, ps, other] \n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAtsushi Kaneko's research works | Kogakuin University and other places (https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Atsushi-Kaneko-70243942)\nciteturn9search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 months ago; Finally, Kouider and Lonc solved the conjecture (even in the stronger Ore-version) in [26]. ... ... Due to the uncertainty of the existence of non-crossing Hamiltonian paths in the general case, researchers have also considered the problem of finding a noncrossing alternating path of length as large as possible [11,15]. ...\n\nOn Decomposition of Triangle-Free Graphs under Degree Constraints\n\n  * Citing Article\n  * January 1998\n\nJournal of Graph Theory\n\nAtsushi Kaneko\n\n> ... For the case of 2-connected graphs G, the conjecture was shown by Kouider in [25]. An Ore-type condition for k = 3 was given in [13]. Finally, Kouider and Lonc solved the conjecture (even in the stronger Ore-version) in [26]. ...\n> \n> Reference:\n> \n> Stability for Vertex Cycle Covers\n\nDegree Sums and Covering Cycles\n\n  * Citing Article\n  * December 1995\n\nJournal of Graph Theory\n\nHikoe Enomoto\n\n·\n\nAts